WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.965
The ransomware rescuers

00:00:01.777 --> 00:00:02.578
were paying the

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.121
ransom

00:00:03.654 --> 00:00:05.045
RansomwareHelp promised

00:00:04.857 --> 00:00:05.682
victims it could

00:00:05.494 --> 00:00:06.814
restore one hundred

00:00:06.626 --> 00:00:07.451
percent of their

00:00:07.263 --> 00:00:08.618
data with advanced

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.727
cryptographic tools

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.635
and told them

00:00:10.446 --> 00:00:11.354
never to pay

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.198
An FBI sting

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:13.953
found the company

00:00:13.765 --> 00:00:14.696
simply paid the

00:00:14.508 --> 00:00:15.462
attackers for a

00:00:15.274 --> 00:00:16.335
decryption key

00:00:16.595 --> 00:00:17.845
then charged victims

00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:18.599
a markup for

00:00:18.411 --> 00:00:19.260
work it never

00:00:19.071 --> 00:00:19.955
performed

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:21.889
Its chief technology

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.410
officer and co-founder

00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:24.613
of a six-year-old

00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:25.497
Florida business

00:00:25.698 --> 00:00:26.606
has now been

00:00:26.418 --> 00:00:27.620
charged with wire

00:00:27.432 --> 00:00:28.115
fraud

00:00:28.638 --> 00:00:29.652
Full story on

00:00:29.463 --> 00:00:30.359
the dashboard
